# oracle: pair_style comb3 polar_off on a small hydrocarbon: two C2H4, two C2H6 and one C3H8 molecule (propane gives C-C-C chains for the radical k and l terms) in a 24 A periodic box (39 atoms, element list C H, so lib.comb3 is read and the radical and torsion paths switch on), 0.2 A random displacement, all charges 0: run 0, then 20 NVE steps; per-atom forces of the final state (dump) and thermo rows
# native: installed lmp (b332f28 build, which includes COMB3). Charges are 0 for C and H (comb3 allows it), so the Coulomb terms are zero by construction.
# Measured error (engine vs native): worst per-atom force relative error 6.1e-12 (atom 29 vy, after 20 steps); worst thermo relative error about 2e-12 (step 0, etotal). The 1e-8 target holds on every row. Radical l-side force and both torsion paths are live on this geometry; the radical k-side force contributes nothing detectable at 1e-8 here (switching it off passes).
# oracle-inputs: w158cb_hc.data
# oracle-potentials: ffield.comb3 lib.comb3
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8
units		metal
atom_style	charge
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
read_data	w158cb_hc.data
displace_atoms all random 0.2 0.2 0.2 4417 units box
pair_style	comb3 polar_off
pair_coeff	* * ffield.comb3 C H
neighbor	2.0 bin
neigh_modify	every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix		1 all nve
timestep        0.00020
thermo_style	custom step temp etotal pe evdwl ecoul press vol lx ly lz
thermo_modify	norm yes format float %.15g
thermo		10
run		0
run		20
